# Market data — large, rebuildable, and partly third-party. Never commit.
#
# `data/*` rather than `data/`: git cannot re-include a file inside a directory
# that is itself excluded, so excluding the CONTENTS is what makes the
# negations below work at all.
data/*
# The runtime summaries ARE the dashboard's data source (~35 KB). Committing
# them puts every state the dashboard ever showed into git history, which no
# API could give you.
!data/runtime/
# The forward session CSVs are the append-only audit trail, and the daily
# commit is what keeps the repo active against GitHub's 60-day disable of
# scheduled workflows on inactive repositories.
!data/sessions/

# Backtest outputs — regenerable from (code, data, config)
results/

# Python
.venv/
venv/
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
*.egg-info/
.pytest_cache/
.ipynb_checkpoints/

# Secrets — broker API keys must never be committed
.env
.env.*
# ...but the template MUST be committed. Without this negation `.env.*` above
# swallows it silently, and a new environment has nothing to copy from.
!.env.example
*.pem
secrets*

# macOS
.DS_Store

# NOTE: config/ and reports/ are intentionally NOT ignored.
#   config/     -> strategy pre-registration + trials.jsonl are the validation record (PROJECT.md §8)
#   reports/    -> data-quality snapshots are small and worth keeping as history

# Shadow/production runtime secrets (never committed)
config/.env.shadow
backups/
